playfair1909 [vi]: Though independent of each other, the clans [a single village may include members of different clans; cf. variables 45 and 47] were in a state of internecine feuds. Retaliation for murder, adultery or insult to any member or members of a Mahari [subclan] was a clan responsibility, and it is interesting to note that in a good many cases was carried on from generation to generation till finally settled. Revenge always resulted in head-hunting which, in course of time, grew as a symbol of their chilvalry.
[It is not clear if the feuds also takes place within a single local community]
